          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nīhāra \"mist, fog, hoar-frost\" is old, in the Rigveda. MW splits it as nī- \"down\" + hāra, pointing to the verb ni-√hṛ, but does not explain the sense, so its formation is uncertain. Hindi kept it as nīhār \"fog, mist\" (CDIAL 7574)."
            }
          ]
        },
